{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md GLOSSARY.md docs/planning/chunks/C32.md docs/architecture/review-protocol.md docs/architecture/review-verdict.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 agent guidance\n\n## Current stage\n\nP01–P07 completed. The owner-authorized P09 integration proceeds under D058/D059\nwhile P08/C26 remains open. C44 attempt-05 passed at 9 in all dimensions and is\nmerged; actual L19 wizard verification passed. C29 attempt-07 was accepted at 8,\nand its restored native coverage must run in the Worf VM before the C29–C32 and\nP09 re-reviews. Read [WORF-START-HERE](docs/planning/WORF-START-HERE.md),\n[status](docs/planning/status.md) and the exact retained verdicts for current state.\nThe approved [C45/P10 brief](docs/planning/C45-draft.md) starts after P09 passes at\n9. Do not re-ask its settled naming, fresh-setup or sequencing decisions.\n\nProduct endpoints are called only within explicit controlled live scope. L19’s\noriginal two plus separately approved third reads are all charged; no additional\nL19 live call is authorized. The next fixture gates need no real credentials.\nDo not copy host Keychains, private manifests, CLI tenant TOMLs or auth profiles.\n\n## Accepted direction\n\n- React presentation hosted by Tauri; focused Rust application implementation.\n- Use the Rust SCM SDK directly; no shipped Node/Bun backend runtime or\n  TypeScript backend workers. Build tooling and React WebView JavaScript are\n  distinct from a shipped backend runtime.\n- Academy owns its learner presentation and hosted learning contracts. Share its\n  React components/themes/shell where suitable; preserve hosted grading/access\n  authority. Academy gamification stays in the Academy feature.\n- Selectively evaluate cdot-framework modules and architecture patterns. Do not\n  carry media generation, commercial billing, MySQL/Redis, or its server stack\n  into the desktop runtime. Preserve upstream provenance/licenses.\n- Cover working v1 behavior in testable slices; classify previews/stubs explicitly.\n- macOS Apple Silicon first; v2 coexists with v1 using independent application,\n  protected-storage, and local-data identities.\n- Rust owns credential access, tenant context, request authority, and reviewed\n  configuration changes. Harness proposals do not authorize Apply.\n- D060 removes alpha import from the one presentation. C45/P10 removes the\n  remaining alpha readers/contracts and starts the new namespace with fresh\n  setup; no alpha/v2 data, credentials or approvals are migrated.\n- Offline local work is supported; no silent replay of remote operations.\n- Remote Gateway usage/cost/budget/limit administration is product functionality,\n  not desktop application monetization.\n\n## Source ownership and working safety\n\n- This repository: `/Users/cdot/development/redtail/prisma-airs-desktop-v2`.\n- Framework reference: `/Users/cdot/development/redtail/ampersand-services`.\n- V1 behavioral reference: `/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-desktop`.\n- Shared Academy: `/Users/cdot/development/redtail/ai-security-academy`.\n- SDK: `airs.coder:/home/cdot/development/cdot65/scm-sdk-rs`.\n- Desktop-capable native Harness source:\n  `/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-harness-desktop-mcp`.\n\nRead applicable guidance before changing another checkout. Preserve active SDK\nwork and user changes. Pin accepted external revisions for reproducible inputs;\ndo not assume evolving worktrees or an older similarly named Harness checkout\nmatch the required contracts. Current research evidence is a snapshot, not live\nqualification. Never read or log credentials for planning.\n\n## Reviews and completion\n\nMost original implementation was Claude Code; the owner authorized Codex for\nthe current integration and remediation. Under D026, every implementation chunk and every phase\n(cumulatively) requires a real independent Codex review scoring at least 9/10 in\narchitecture, behavior, authority_security, validation and overall, with empty\nrequired_fixes, blockers and evidence_gaps. Historical G00/G01 Claude reviews\nare retained unchanged and cover only their recorded inputs.\nUnder D034 (superseding D032 for chunks) a chunk completes on a review scoring\nat least 8 in all five dimensions with no blockers (`xtask complete\n--owner-accept REASON`); the ledger records the acceptance and every accepted\nfailure (required fixes, evidence gaps). Phase reviews still need 9/10 with no\nowner acceptance, and every chunk of the phase accepted below 9 must first be\nremediated and re-reviewed to a passing 9/10 (a new generation, later chunks\nnot reopened); `xtask complete` enforces both.\nRetain source/dependency fingerprints, raw verdicts, commands, test results, and\nremediation attempts. Re-review changed source. Never fabricate a score, substitute\nself-review, edit a verdict, or treat favorable scores as evidence that unrun tests\npassed. A queue acknowledgement or process exit status is not a verdict.\n\nFollow `docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`, the ordered C01–C26 instructions,\nreview/test/dependency/release contracts and canonical prompts. G01 specifies\nconcrete interfaces and exact native/check commands before implementation.\nDo not invent these future gates as completed results.\nKeep sensitive raw evidence private and repository records redacted.\n\nThe owner specified `ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot/prisma-airs-desktop-v2.git` as\nthis repository's destination. Use normal pushes only when publication is within\nthe active task; do not force-push, rewrite unrelated repositories, promote v2\nover v1, or publish application releases during planning.\n# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 domain vocabulary\n\nThese terms name the desktop product and its native authority concepts.\nMechanisms, wire formats and transition rules belong in the selected design.\n\n## Language\n\n**Tenant profile**: An application-owned configuration for a Prisma AIRS tenant,\nincluding its label, endpoints, and protected credential references. A scan-only\nprofile does not require management OAuth credentials. A profile is not an\nAcademy learner account or a Gateway workspace.\n\n**Credential capability**: The specific operations a credential can authorize,\nsuch as scanning, management, inference, or workspace MCP. Possessing one\ncapability does not establish another; configuration keeps them explicit.\n\n**Gateway workspace**: A remote AI Gateway administrative/inference context within\nthe selected tenant profile. It is distinct from a local filesystem project.\n\n**Configuration review**: An operator-visible proposal for an AIRS configuration\nchange, bound to the current tenant, credential context, target resource, and\ndraft. Rust owns its validity. Displaying or importing a proposal does not grant\npermission to apply it.\n\n**Remote outcome**: What is known about an attempted remote action: not sent,\nrejected, completed as established by evidence, or unknown. Local timeout,\ncancellation, and disconnection do not establish remote rollback.\n\n**Academy feature**: The learner experience within the broader desktop app.\nPresentation is shared with Academy; remote learning contracts remain hosted.\nLearning progression, XP, cosmetic credits, awards, and other gamification stay\nwithin this feature.\n\n**Academy learner account**: The remote learning identity owning progress,\nassessments, certificates, and account-scoped local drafts/downloads. It is\nindependent of the selected Prisma AIRS tenant and Harness inference sign-in.\n\n**Shared presentation**: React controls, themes, and shell layout reused from the\nAcademy-owned source. Sharing appearance does not share learner authority,\ngamification effects, manager routes, or browser-session assumptions globally.\n\n**Harness**: The assistant feature using the native Rust agent engine and\ndesktop-owned lifecycle, credential grants, reviews, and protected history.\nThe SCM SDK is a separate dependency, not the Harness engine.\n\n**Project scope**: The explicitly selected local filesystem scope and approved\ntool permissions available to a Harness conversation. Preserve the existing\nrestrictions initially; a transcript is not permission to restore approvals.\n\n**MCP grant**: A desktop-owned authorization context for a specific remote MCP\nbinding. Inference sign-in is separate. Discovery does not establish execution;\nexecution evidence must correspond to the actual approved call.\n\n**Historical conversation**: Saved user work that can be inspected after import.\nResumption requires separate context/protocol compatibility validation. It never\nrestores pending approvals or old authentication sessions.\n\n**Billing**: Desktop commercial charging/monetization machinery, excluded from\nv2. Remote Gateway usage/cost/budget/limit administration remains product\nfunctionality. Academy's earned learning economy remains Academy-local.\n\n**Shipped backend runtime**: Executables/workers required by the installed app's\nbackend. Node/Bun and TypeScript backend workers are excluded. Build-time JS\ntooling and React JavaScript executing in the WebView are separate concepts.\n\n**Parity**: Coverage of agreed working v1 behavior with new v2 evidence. V1 source\nimplementation, retained fixture/contract results, retained live evidence, and\nv2 installed-artifact results are distinct. Replacing a preview/stub with a live\nfeature is scope expansion, not implicit parity work.\n\n**Authority principal**: The native-established operator or restricted Harness\nidentity on whose behalf desktop work is requested. A claimed identity in a\nrequest is not an Authority principal.\n\n**Authority handle**: A principal-scoped entry to native desktop operations and\nobservations. Possessing an operation reference does not expand its authority.\n\n**Intent**: A typed request for a specific desktop action under the caller's\ncurrent authority. It is distinct from a Harness proposal or an arbitrary remote\nrequest.\n\n**Receipt**: Native acknowledgement that an Intent was admitted, with its request\nor operation reference. It is not evidence of operator confirmation or remote\ncompletion.\n\n**Refusal**: Native rejection of an Intent before admission under the requested\nauthority. A remote action's failure is a Remote outcome instead.\n\n**ViewScope**: The product context a caller asks to observe, such as a learner\naccount, tenant workspace or Harness conversation. Native authority determines\nwhich part is visible to that caller.\n\n**Observation**: A scoped redacted view of native desktop state and operation\nprogress. It confers no execution or credential authority.\n\n**ContextRef**: A native reference to the particular product context presented\nto the caller. Returning to the same tenant or account does not revive retired\nauthority.\n\n**Delivery session**: The current native-registered channel for one caller's\nIntent deliveries. It is separate from tenant, learner or inference identity.\n\n**Delivery sequence**: The order identity of an Intent within its Delivery session,\nused to distinguish duplicate delivery from an explicit new action.\n_Avoid_: Business retry, authorization token\n\n**Native-owned payload reference**: A scoped reference to staged desktop input\nwhose ownership and content are known natively. It is not permission to read an\narbitrary filesystem path.\n\n**Reviewed**: A Configuration review whose captured proposal remains eligible for\noperator confirmation.\n\n**Confirming**: A Configuration review currently awaiting the native operator's\nanswer for that specific proposal.\n\n**Consumed**: A Configuration review already committed to its single admitted\noperation. Failure of that operation does not make the review reusable.\n\n**Queued**: An admitted desktop operation whose remote dispatch has not been\nclaimed.\n\n**DispatchClaimed**: A desktop operation for which remote dispatch may have begun.\nLocal cancellation at this stage does not prove NotSent.\n\n**Settled**: A desktop operation with a recorded terminal local result and its\ncurrent Remote outcome. Later reconciliation may refine knowledge of that outcome.\n\n**Harness grant**: Native authority for one verified inference identity and its\napproved tenant/workspace/origin context. Rotating that identity's token material\nis distinct from replacing or revoking the Harness grant.\n\n**Grant epoch**: The particular lifetime of a native grant's authority. Retired\nauthority stays retired even when an equivalent identity is selected again.\n\n**One-time secret receipt**: The operator-scoped acknowledgement holding newly\nissued secret material for its explicit transient reveal. It is separate from a\nstored credential lookup.\n\n**Editor lease**: The hold on the reviewed document while native operator\nconfirmation is pending. A changed document or context invalidates that hold.\ncat: docs/architecture/review-protocol.md: No such file or directory\n# C32 — Harness re-skin and lifecycle fixtures\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C31.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe Harness renders in the new shell on the existing engine, sessions and decision model, with the three lifecycle fixtures as regression tests and contextual navigation for ended investigations.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC31; screens/harness.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Harness screen in the layout rhythm: title row, conversation rail, transcript, composer, prerequisites checklist.\n2. Lifecycle fixtures blocks, mcp, keys in the contracts package with approve, decline, end and follow-up paths; all three are read-only tool calls (the mcp lifecycle reads `GatewayRead::McpServers`, P16; the keys lifecycle refuses to rotate and hands off, V2-T18). The existing C21 rule stands: the core decides from the tool's write flag whether the native confirmation sheet is required; no P09 fixture adds a write-capable call.\n3. `endConversation` seals the session and returns an archive id; transient hint for ended-conversation navigation; first send on a fresh tenant creates a user conversation.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- I1 pending-decision guard end to end (V2-N01), I12 (V2-T13); every lifecycle path tested; engine pin check unchanged.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nFixture engine only; no live Harness runs (L16/L17 belong to C26).\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 independent review verdict\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"request_id\",\n    \"attempt_id\",\n    \"subject\",\n    \"fingerprints\",\n    \"scores\",\n    \"required_fixes\",\n    \"blockers\",\n    \"evidence_gaps\",\n    \"optional_suggestions\",\n    \"limitations\",\n    \"inspected_files\",\n    \"recommendation\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"request_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"attempt_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Chunk C01-C44 or phase P01-P09 under review\"\n    },\n    \"fingerprints\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"source\",\n        \"dependencies\",\n        \"build_flags\",\n        \"evidence\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"source\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"dependencies\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"build_flags\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"evidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"scores\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"architecture\",\n        \"behavior\",\n        \"authority_security\",\n        \"validation\",\n        \"overall\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"architecture\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"behavior\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"authority_security\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"validation\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        },\n        \"overall\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"minimum\": 1,\n          \"maximum\": 10\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"required_fixes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"blockers\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"evidence_gaps\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"optional_suggestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"limitations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"inspected_files\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"recommendation\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"pass\",\n        \"fail\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
