sions.md:1364:## D046 — The native Harness engine: sealed resource, lifecycle and the C19 conversation\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:1498:## D047 — Harness company sign-in, renewal and protected history\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:1504:Harness: the Gateway workspace and runtime endpoint the token is for, and\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:1711:## D048 — Harness desktop tools, project folder, approvals and proposals\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:1838:## D049 — Workspace MCP servers for the Harness: catalog, desktop OAuth, grants and approval\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:1997:## D050 — Reviewed v1 import: source contract, mapping, receipts and rollback\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2128:  Harness history list, the API Client's recent list, Academy's kept\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2213:## D051 — Local redacted diagnostics: typed events, retention, export and reset\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2276:## D052 — C25 scope reduction: Gateway workspace provisioning (W37, W39)\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2298:## D053 — C25 scope reduction: five blocked live checks\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2313:## D054 — scm-sdk 0.2.4\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2324:## D055 — C25 review attempt-01: deferrals and a waived cleanup\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2328:1. **L16 and L17's Harness-run checks are C26's.** L16 (the Harness over\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2331:   (W48) run inside the Harness engine, which runs only in the signed app.\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2344:## D056 — Academy live follow-ups move to 2.1.0; stable is 2.0.0\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2360:   runs them. C25 stays complete at its D034 chunk gate. The P08 phase\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2363:## D057 — C26 attempt 01: installed-acceptance defects and the Git rule\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2379:2. **F05 (Harness company sign-in).** Company sign-in was reachable only\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2381:   before that mentioned it. The Harness now shows a \"what you need first\"\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2391:## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2393:Accepted by the owner on 2026-10-26 (\"I accept it as written\"), with authority to implement P09 end to end autonomously and to proceed with C28 while C26 remains in progress; every chunk is reviewed until it scores 9 in every dimension.\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2397:Native\", and iterated its prototype (R2App, R2Onboard, R2Harness ×3,\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2407:   phase P09 chunks C27–C34 (see the chunk index). The first implementation\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2413:3. D014 holds: secrets enter only through the host secret sheet and vault;\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2419:   tenant switch is refused by the core while a Harness decision is pending;\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2443:   C28–C34 follow D034.\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2446:   redacted wire data; English only in P09; chunks commit on main except C34.\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2451:## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2454:accepted; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md`). C32 had taken twenty review rounds\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2458:- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2466:  the full fixture suite, the Codex review), accepted at 8 under D032/D034; the\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2471:- Chunks: C35 shell, C36 Home, C37 Inbox fix-up, C38 Harness, C39 Administration\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2474:  over the existing state machine, C44 legacy removal on a branch and the P09\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2477:## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2490:## Interview exit and remaining evidence\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2502:## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2507:- Still to decide the same way, in a follow-up chunk the owner names (proposed C45): the core's alpha-import intents and reader (`import_v1_domain`, the `V1Import*` intents, the host adapters), Settings' file-based \"Import tenant profiles\" and the API Client's \"Import v1 API Client profile\" adoption, which are alpha-import surfaces too; their removal changes contracts and earlier chunks' tests and is not done inside the P09 closure.\ndocs/planning/decisions.md:2508:- Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:8:## Source ownership\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:15:| Native Harness | 9331a5839bc6a763d94dee7584746f58bbbe1181 | Desktop-capable native engine/protocol input            |\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:27:## C01 resolved inputs\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:48:## Required gates\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:81:- **Harness:** retain the desktop-capable native engine/protocol after source and\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:97:  for Academy device authorization, Harness company SSO and MCP. Responsible\ndocs/planning/dependencies.md:105:## Official host references\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:9:## Core authority and SDK\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:39:## Presentation and Academy\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:61:## Workflows and Harness\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:71:- **T15 Harness process:** actual native binary and bounded bootstrap/JSONL\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:75:- **T16 Harness authority:** typed investigation/proposal tools, active-draft\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:86:## Import, quality, and artifacts\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:97:  and scan/large-list/streaming/Harness memory, main-thread responsiveness, file\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:113:  Harness history, configuration drafts, and Academy work. Mark remote data as\ndocs/planning/test-catalogue.md:120:## Performance budget governance\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
