{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'it\\\\(|test\\\\(|describe\\\\(' apps/desktop/src/v2/harness/harness.test.tsx && cat packages/desktop-contracts/fixtures/wire/harness-lifecycle-keys.json\"","aggregated_output":"142:describe('v2 Harness', () => {\n143:    it('ships lifecycle fixtures the core contract accepts at every step', () => {\n154:        it(`${l.lifecycle}: the read-only call is approved in the page, its follow-up opens only a review, and ending seals the conversation (V2-T17)`, async () => {\n190:        it(`${l.lifecycle}: declining records the decision and the assistant's declined text, with no follow-up (V2-T17)`, async () => {\n203:    it('keys: the Harness refuses to rotate and hands off; the follow-up follows the rotation stage and never dispatches a mutation (V2-T18)', async () => {\n231:    it('a fresh tenant shows no seeded conversation; its first send starts a user conversation and sends the message once it is ready (V2-T13, I12)', async () => {\n256:    it('sending after a conversation ended clears it and starts a new one', async () => {\n267:    it('contextual navigation into an ended conversation shows the hint; it opens the saved transcript or prefills a new investigation, and clears on navigation', async () => {\n298:    it('a contextual restart of the ended conversation prefills its whole opening question, never its shortened title; a draft is kept and nothing is sent (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n319:    it('a contextual restart of an archived conversation reads its record for the whole opening question; a draft is kept and nothing is sent (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n344:    it('says when the opening question is not known, or its record could not be read, and never substitutes the title (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n384:    it('a repeated read failure of an archived record settles each read by its receipt: loading ends, the failure is said, retry works, the draft stays and nothing starts (attempt-13 R1)', async () => {\n412:    it('a contextual arrival waits for the saved conversations to be listed: the hint appears once its record is, the draft stays and nothing starts (attempt-14 R1)', async () => {\n441:    it('a pending contextual arrival is cancelled by navigation or another workspace, and says when its record is not listed or cannot be (attempt-14 R1)', async () => {\n491:    it('choosing New investigation while an archived record is read retires the contextual restart: its late success or failure changes neither the draft nor the choice (attempt-15 R1)', async () => {\n522:    it('a read refused after the operator chose another investigation says nothing over it (attempt-16 S1)', async () => {\n557:    it('keeps the prerequisites checklist until every one is satisfied', async () => {\n567:    it('keeps the C19–C22 controls: the project, sign-in and MCP panels, saved-conversation management, and the write confirmation after a renewal', async () => {\n586:    it('says when a decision may change things: approving asks for the system confirmation, never in-page consent alone (R1)', async () => {\n608:    it('keeps the first message until a conversation takes it: refused, failed startup and a replacement never lose it or send it elsewhere (R2)', async () => {\n645:    it('a new investigation while one runs ends it and sends to a different conversation; the contextual restart shows its opening question (R3)', async () => {\n674:    it('a pending decision holds a new investigation back', async () => {\n681:    it('a pending decision holds a contextual restart back without losing its hint; an unconfirmed read is never called a failure', async () => {\n707:    it('returns an unsent message to the box with the sign-in failure, and resends nothing (R4)', async () => {\n718:    it('shows how the conversation stands: a failed start, a cut or failed answer, a failed cleanup and an unsaved transcript are never presented as complete or saved (R5)', async () => {\n742:    it('keeps each draft in its tenant, workspace and conversation across navigation and a tenant round trip, sending nothing by itself (R6)', async () => {\n759:    it('keeps the box and the new-investigation choice by workspace ID across navigation and an A/B/A that retires the conversation (attempt-02/03 R1)', async () => {\n781:    it('retires a first send whose conversation ends before it is ready, or whose start is unconfirmed: text kept, controls usable, nothing sent (attempt-02 R2)', async () => {\n806:    it('clears only the submitted text: an edit made while the first send waits, or while a message is delivered, stays (attempt-02 R3)', async () => {\n834:    it('keeps both a returned message and the draft typed meanwhile: the message goes under Not sent with a way back into the box (attempt-02/03 R4)', async () => {\n851:    it('keeps every edit across the starting snapshot: edits before and after it stay in the one box (attempt-03 R2)', async () => {\n868:    it('says truthfully where an unsent first message is: still in the box, or kept under Not sent when the box changed (attempt-03 R3)', async () => {\n897:    it('one Send starts at most one conversation and delivers once, even when the clear publishes before its receipt (attempt-03 R4)', async () => {\n925:    it('keeps a refused or undelivered follow-up beside the edit made while it was delivered, and resends nothing (attempt-04 R1)', async () => {\n959:    it('never calls an unconfirmed send \"not sent\": only the core\\'s word that it took that send settles it, never matching text, and nothing is resent (attempt-04 R2, attempt-16 R1)', async () => {\n981:    it('identical unconfirmed sends in two conversations are settled each by its own conversation only (attempt-06 R1)', async () => {\n1005:    it('two identical unconfirmed sends are settled each by its own ID, once, across renders and a remount (attempt-07 R1, attempt-10 R1)', async () => {\n1029:    it('an admitted retry never settles the unconfirmed original: only the original\\'s own ID does (attempt-08 R1, attempt-09 R1)', async () => {\n1053:    it('an admitted send\\'s delayed entry never settles a later identical unconfirmed send; that send\\'s own ID settles it once (attempt-16 R1)', async () => {\n1090:    it('a send whose receipt was lost and that the core then gave back is never taken as delivered: its exact text stays in the box or under Not sent (attempt-17 R1)', async () => {\n1156:    it('a receipt that arrives after the core gave its send back never clears the returned text, on either send path (attempt-18 R1)', async () => {\n1246:    it('a pending report is never final: a send later given back keeps its exact text beside newer edits, on both send paths and through an A/B/A that retires its conversation (attempt-19 R1)', async () => {\n1309:    it('the rail keeps the conversation\\'s title from its opening after the transcript dropped it, also once ended (attempt-18 R2)', async () => {\n1328:    it('settles an unconfirmed send by the core\\'s word even when the transcript is at its bounds and dropped its oldest entries (attempt-11 R1)', async () => {\n1351:    it('a lost start receipt is never \"no conversation started\": the message stays, sent nowhere (attempt-04 R2, lost start receipt)', async () => {\n1370:    it('settles an unconfirmed send only by a message its own conversation added after it: a repeated prompt or another conversation settles nothing (attempt-05 R1)', async () => {\n1397:    it('a retry whose receipt is lost moves a refused message from Not sent to Not confirmed, truthfully (attempt-05 R2)', async () => {\n1433:    it('a later refused retry never downgrades an earlier unconfirmed send (attempt-06 R1)', async () => {\n1465:    it('confirms an ended conversation with a toast bound to its tenant and context (I10)', async () => {\n1478:    it('a retry whose entry arrives before its receipt never settles the unconfirmed original either (attempt-09 R1)', async () => {\n1517:    it('draws the board: the title band with End conversation, the 244px rail of saved conversations, the transcript with its composer, and the Decisions aside holding the decision (C38)', async () => {\n1550:    it('tells the aside what it cannot decide yet, and names the workspace MCP servers with their standing (C38)', async () => {\n1591:    it('says what the MCP summary knows: not read, reading, failed, partial; every server that is on is listed and the rest are counted (attempt-01 R1)', async () => {\n1612:    it('chooses a folder, names a refused one, allows changes in it and removes it, through the v2 project panel (C21, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1638:    it('keeps a lost receipt as Not confirmed in the v2 panels, naming the action; the next snapshot settles what happened and the page resends nothing (attempt-02 R1)', async () => {\n1713:    it('sets up company sign-in, signs in through the browser, chooses the credential and signs out, through the v2 sign-in panel; a refused save is named (C20, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1762:    it('reads the MCP catalog, turns servers on, signs in and out, says why a server cannot be used and keeps at most eight on, through the v2 MCP panel (C22, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1844:    it('lists, opens, continues, exports and deletes saved conversations, says why one cannot be continued, names unreadable ones and a locked store, through the v2 history panel (C20, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n{\n  \"lifecycle\": \"keys\",\n  \"question\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n  \"steps\": {\n    \"asking\": {\n      \"id\": \"op-43\",\n      \"workspace\": {\n        \"id\": \"16f7e90d-382a-4e78-b577-1b01eb5f8297\",\n        \"name\": \"Team A\",\n        \"slug\": \"team-a\",\n        \"scopeName\": \"scope-team-a\"\n      },\n      \"endpoint\": \"https://gateway.example/rt/v1\",\n      \"phase\": \"answering\",\n      \"failure\": null,\n      \"stop\": null,\n      \"entries\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1\",\n          \"role\": \"operator\",\n          \"text\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/call-1\",\n          \"role\": \"tool\",\n          \"text\": \"Read the API keys inventory\",\n          \"state\": \"streaming\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"lastTurn\": null,\n      \"usage\": null,\n      \"cleanup\": null,\n      \"runtimeVersion\": \"0.104.0\",\n      \"source\": \"workspaceKey\",\n      \"historyId\": \"7c2a4e9d-3f5b-4c8d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f\",\n      \"savedAt\": null,\n      \"saveFailure\": null,\n      \"unsent\": null,\n      \"signInFailure\": null,\n      \"project\": null,\n      \"write\": false,\n      \"approvals\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7\",\n          \"kind\": \"desktopRead\",\n          \"command\": null,\n          \"cwd\": null,\n          \"reason\": null,\n          \"files\": [],\n          \"server\": \"airs_desktop\",\n          \"tool\": \"inventory\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"resource\\\":\\\"apiKeys\\\",\\\"limit\\\":25}\",\n          \"effect\": \"readOnly\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"proposals\": [],\n      \"mcp\": [],\n      \"opening\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\"\n    },\n    \"approved\": {\n      \"id\": \"op-43\",\n      \"workspace\": {\n        \"id\": \"16f7e90d-382a-4e78-b577-1b01eb5f8297\",\n        \"name\": \"Team A\",\n        \"slug\": \"team-a\",\n        \"scopeName\": \"scope-team-a\"\n      },\n      \"endpoint\": \"https://gateway.example/rt/v1\",\n      \"phase\": \"ready\",\n      \"failure\": null,\n      \"stop\": null,\n      \"entries\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1\",\n          \"role\": \"operator\",\n          \"text\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/call-1\",\n          \"role\": \"tool\",\n          \"text\": \"Read the API keys inventory\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/a-1\",\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"text\": \"One key expires before the audit: 'Support key' of support-copilot, on 2026-11-20. I will not rotate it: rotation is a write; it goes through Administration and a review.\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/a-2\",\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"text\": \"I staged the start of its rotation (an additional key for support-copilot) for your review in Administration. Nothing is issued until you confirm it there.\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"lastTurn\": \"completed\",\n      \"usage\": null,\n      \"cleanup\": null,\n      \"runtimeVersion\": \"0.104.0\",\n      \"source\": \"workspaceKey\",\n      \"historyId\": \"7c2a4e9d-3f5b-4c8d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f\",\n      \"savedAt\": 1793230000,\n      \"saveFailure\": null,\n      \"unsent\": null,\n      \"signInFailure\": null,\n      \"project\": null,\n      \"write\": false,\n      \"approvals\": [],\n      \"proposals\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"P-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Start the rotation of support-copilot's key in Administration\",\n          \"draft\": {\n            \"kind\": \"apiKeys\",\n            \"action\": \"version\",\n            \"target\": \"key-1\",\n            \"body\": \"{\\\"cust_app\\\":\\\"support-copilot\\\",\\\"cust_env\\\":\\\"production\\\",\\\"cust_cloud_provider\\\":\\\"aws\\\",\\\"api_key_name\\\":\\\"Support key 2\\\",\\\"dp_name\\\":\\\"dp-1\\\",\\\"revoked\\\":false,\\\"rotation_time_interval\\\":30,\\\"rotation_time_unit\\\":\\\"days\\\"}\"\n          },\n          \"state\": \"staged\",\n          \"review\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"mcp\": [],\n      \"opening\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\"\n    },\n    \"declined\": {\n      \"id\": \"op-43\",\n      \"workspace\": {\n        \"id\": \"16f7e90d-382a-4e78-b577-1b01eb5f8297\",\n        \"name\": \"Team A\",\n        \"slug\": \"team-a\",\n        \"scopeName\": \"scope-team-a\"\n      },\n      \"endpoint\": \"https://gateway.example/rt/v1\",\n      \"phase\": \"ready\",\n      \"failure\": null,\n      \"stop\": null,\n      \"entries\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1\",\n          \"role\": \"operator\",\n          \"text\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/call-1\",\n          \"role\": \"tool\",\n          \"text\": \"Read the API keys inventory\",\n          \"state\": \"declined\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/a-1\",\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"text\": \"You declined the read, so nothing was read. I cannot tell which keys expire without the key inventory.\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"lastTurn\": \"completed\",\n      \"usage\": null,\n      \"cleanup\": null,\n      \"runtimeVersion\": \"0.104.0\",\n      \"source\": \"workspaceKey\",\n      \"historyId\": \"7c2a4e9d-3f5b-4c8d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f\",\n      \"savedAt\": 1793230000,\n      \"saveFailure\": null,\n      \"unsent\": null,\n      \"signInFailure\": null,\n      \"project\": null,\n      \"write\": false,\n      \"approvals\": [],\n      \"proposals\": [],\n      \"mcp\": [],\n      \"opening\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\"\n    },\n    \"ended\": {\n      \"id\": \"op-43\",\n      \"workspace\": {\n        \"id\": \"16f7e90d-382a-4e78-b577-1b01eb5f8297\",\n        \"name\": \"Team A\",\n        \"slug\": \"team-a\",\n        \"scopeName\": \"scope-team-a\"\n      },\n      \"endpoint\": \"https://gateway.example/rt/v1\",\n      \"phase\": \"ended\",\n      \"failure\": null,\n      \"stop\": \"ended\",\n      \"entries\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1\",\n          \"role\": \"operator\",\n          \"text\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/call-1\",\n          \"role\": \"tool\",\n          \"text\": \"Read the API keys inventory\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/a-1\",\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"text\": \"One key expires before the audit: 'Support key' of support-copilot, on 2026-11-20. I will not rotate it: rotation is a write; it goes through Administration and a review.\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"u-1/a-2\",\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"text\": \"I staged the start of its rotation (an additional key for support-copilot) for your review in Administration. Nothing is issued until you confirm it there.\",\n          \"state\": \"complete\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"lastTurn\": \"completed\",\n      \"usage\": null,\n      \"cleanup\": \"graceful\",\n      \"runtimeVersion\": \"0.104.0\",\n      \"source\": \"workspaceKey\",\n      \"historyId\": \"7c2a4e9d-3f5b-4c8d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f\",\n      \"savedAt\": 1793230000,\n      \"saveFailure\": null,\n      \"unsent\": null,\n      \"signInFailure\": null,\n      \"project\": null,\n      \"write\": false,\n      \"approvals\": [],\n      \"proposals\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"P-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Start the rotation of support-copilot's key in Administration\",\n          \"draft\": {\n            \"kind\": \"apiKeys\",\n            \"action\": \"version\",\n            \"target\": \"key-1\",\n            \"body\": \"{\\\"cust_app\\\":\\\"support-copilot\\\",\\\"cust_env\\\":\\\"production\\\",\\\"cust_cloud_provider\\\":\\\"aws\\\",\\\"api_key_name\\\":\\\"Support key 2\\\",\\\"dp_name\\\":\\\"dp-1\\\",\\\"revoked\\\":false,\\\"rotation_time_interval\\\":30,\\\"rotation_time_unit\\\":\\\"days\\\"}\"\n          },\n          \"state\": \"staged\",\n          \"review\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"mcp\": [],\n      \"opening\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"saved\": {\n    \"id\": \"7c2a4e9d-3f5b-4c8d-8e1f-2a3b4c5d6e7f\",\n    \"title\": \"Which API keys expire before the audit, and can you rotate them?\",\n    \"updated\": 1793230000,\n    \"entries\": 4,\n    \"source\": \"workspaceKey\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
